== Variants ==
=== Attack Fly ===
{{infobox monster
 | name        = Attack Fly
 | id          = 18
 | base hp     = 5
 | environment = {{floor|Basement}}{{floor|Cellar}}{{floor|Burning Basement}}<br>{{floor|Dross}}<br>{{floor|Caves}}{{floor|Catacombs}}{{floor|Flooded Caves}}<br>{{floor|Depths}}{{floor|Necropolis}}{{floor|Dank Depths}}<br>{{floor|Womb}}{{floor|Utero}}{{floor|Scarred Womb}}<br>{{floor|Chest}}<br>{{room|boss}}{{room|challenge}}{{room|vault}}{{room|I AM ERROR}}{{room|treasure}}<br>{{dlc|nr}}<br>{{room|crawl space}}
 | behavior    = Red fly that follows Isaac and deals contact damage.
}}

'''Attack Flies''' are red and black flashing flies that will chase Isaac, dealing contact damage.

Weirdly, while they can easily hit Isaac from the left or right, they have great difficulty hitting him from the top or bottom.

==== Notes ====
* Attack Flies turn into regular Flies if Isaac has {{i|Skatole}}. However, they take a small amount of time to convert into Flies, so it is possible for Isaac to be damaged if the player is not careful.
* {{e|Hive}}s can spit out attack flies that die upon touching Isaac, but the ones spawned upon the monster's death do not.
* {{e|The Duke of Flies}} can spit out normal and larger versions of Attack Flies that have 10 base HP. Both of these Attack Flies die upon touching Isaac, but the ones spawned upon the boss's death do not.
* {{e|The Husk}} can spit out attack flies that die upon touching Isaac, but the ones spawned upon the boss's death do not. 
* {{e|Gurdy}} can spawn weaker versions of Attack Flies that only have 3 base HP and die upon touching Isaac.
{{clear}}

=== Ring Fly ===
