== Trivia ==
* The Black Fly has the lowest health of any enemy in the game, tied with the {{e|Corn}}.
* Eternal Flies were first added to the ''Wrath of the Lamb'' DLC for the original ''Binding of Isaac'' game.
** Before ''Rebirth'', Eternal Flies simply became vulnerable and chased the player rather than turning into an Attack Fly.
* There is a variant of [[enboi:Moter|Moters]] in the ''Eternal Edition'' of the original ''The Binding of Isaac'' that resembles a ball of 4 Attack Flies, or 2 Moters stuck to each other. This enemy does not appear in ''Rebirth'', likely due to being added in said ''Eternal Edition'' update that was added a while after the release of ''Rebirth''.
* In a Q&A Reddit thread by [[Edmund McMillen]], Edmund confirmed that the species of flies in ''The Binding of Isaac'' are [[Wikipedia:Housefly|house flies]] and [[Wikipedia:Botfly|botflies]].<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/bindingofisaac/comments/g854b5/tapeworm_kickstarter_four_souls_and_general_isaac/</ref>
* {{dlc|r}} The [[Anti:Willo|Willo]] originates from the ''Antibirth'' mod.
* The name Willo might be a reference to Will'o the Wisps, atmospheric ghost lights seen at night, especially over bogs, swamps or marshes.
* Although Army Flies were known to be revealed during Repentance's first PAX session, it was in fact first revealed in the [https://blog.antibirth.com/ latest blog of a now-canceled update for the Antibirth mod] back in December 21, 2017.

